{#
  Homepage, rewritten 2026-09-30 (Bruce). The site had become a single-product
  page for Pipeworx, which undersold the company: Pipeworx is one of two pieces
  of infrastructure, and the services built on top are the evidence that the
  infrastructure works.

  THE EDITORIAL RULE, and it decides what belongs here:
  Pipeworx and NoHumans are INFRASTRUCTURE. Everything else is PROOF. A new
  product earns a place on this page by answering "what does this demonstrate
  about making agents more useful?" — not by having been built.

  NO HARDCODED COUNTS. Numbers come from registry.pipeworx.io/stats.json at
  runtime (see [data-stat] in main.js). A figure typed into this file starts
  rotting the day it ships, and this site has no access to the live catalog at
  build time. The fallbacks in the markup are deliberately round and stale-safe.

  The worked example is a REAL captured run, labelled as recorded. Do not
  replace it with a prettier invented one — the whole argument on this page is
  that an answer can be traced, so a fabricated trace would be self-defeating.
#}

